-- title:
--   Attachment image maps away from critical face weights
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $V$ a finite vertex set with a fixed injective ordering rank, $K$ a finite downward-closed face family, and $f$ a face-monotone real filtration. Fix $i\in V$, any integer multidegree $b$ on $V\setminus\{i\}$, and $q\in\mathbb N$. Let $I_b^q(t)$ be the literal linear range of the original homogeneous deletion-to-link local-cohomology attachment map at $t$, with the original link restriction restricted to this range as structure map.
--
--   The finite set of critical values is $C=\{f(F):F\in K\}$, including the empty-face weight when the empty face is present. If $s\le t$ and $C\cap(s,t]=\varnothing$, then
--   $$I_b^q(t)\longrightarrow I_b^q(s)$$
--   is an isomorphism. The half-open interval agrees with the sublevel convention $f(F)\le t$. No sign or nonvanishing condition is imposed on $b$. The statement includes $s=t$, $q=0$, ghosts, void complexes and an empty complement. It establishes finite critical-level behavior of the actual image maps.
-- source:
--   https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02858v1, Sections 3 and 4, finite face-weight filtrations and attachment image persistence; supporting finite-level lemma for Corollary 4.4. Certified Lean source: Solutions/LPCA_AttachmentFiniteLevels.lean, selected declarations in lines 26–40; source SHA-256 e8e6cd14cc50f0b19bf8459c84a3900f8e635872af6ac42a34d49f45ce30f3ec; source certificate Sapelo2 job 49172236.

